{"content":{"id":21446,"headline":"Innovative Immunotherapy for Canine Lung Metastases: The CAALM Study","tagline":"Pioneering hope for dogs with metastatic cancer","description":"<p>The <strong>CAALM Study</strong> is evaluating the safety, tolerability, and preliminary efficacy of a novel dog PDL1 antibody (UCD-PDL1). This cutting-edge trial seeks to optimize dosing while exploring the antibody’s potential to improve survival outcomes for dogs with oral melanoma that has spread to the lungs.</p>","requirements":"<p><strong>Eligible Dogs:</strong></p><ol><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Weight: &gt; 15 kg (33 lbs) and &lt; 36 kg (79 lbs)</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Confirmed diagnosis of oral melanoma (via cytology or biopsy)</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Presence of one or more lung nodules consistent with metastatic disease</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Expected survival of &gt; 4 weeks</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Other eligibility requirements will be assessed at the first visit</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Caregivers:</strong></p><ol><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Must be at least 18 years old, able to provide informed consent, and adhere to the study protocol.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Time Commitment:</strong></p><p>Participation involves up to 6 biweekly treatments over a <strong>98-day study period</strong>, including follow-up visits and monitoring.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Adherence to Protocol:</strong></p><p>Owners must monitor their dog’s health, attend scheduled visits at UC Davis School of Veterinary Medicine, and provide accurate updates through questionnaires and check-ins.</p>","who_can_participate":"<p><strong>Eligible Dogs:</strong></p><ol><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Weight: &gt; 15 kg (33 lbs) and &lt; 36 kg (79 lbs)</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Confirmed diagnosis of oral melanoma (via cytology or biopsy)</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Presence of one or more lung nodules consistent with metastatic disease</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Expected survival of &gt; 4 weeks</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Other eligibility requirements will be assessed at the first visit</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Eligible Owners:</strong></p><ol><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>At least 18 years old and able to adhere to the study’s requirements, including appointments and questionnaires.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Exclusion Criteria:</strong></p><ol><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Dogs are not eligible if they:</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Have received prior checkpoint inhibitor therapy.</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Have undergone recent chemotherapy, immunotherapy, or corticosteroid treatment within two weeks of Day 0.</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Present with uncontrolled medical conditions that could interfere with treatment or data interpretation.</li></ol>","benefits_and_risks":"<p><strong>Benefits:</strong></p><ol><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Access to cutting-edge immunotherapy at no cost, including diagnostics, imaging, and antibody treatments.</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Contribution to advancing cancer treatment for dogs through groundbreaking research.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Risks:</strong></p><ol><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Possible side effects of the investigational antibody, such as infusion-related reactions or changes in laboratory test values.</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span>Stress associated with diagnostic tests, treatment, and clinic visits.</li></ol><p><br></p>","video_url":"","age_range":"","keywords":["Canine","Cancer","Mets","lung","Lung Metastases"],"study_type":"Intervention","time_commitment":"Participation involves up to 6 biweekly treatments over a 98-day study period, including follow-up visits and monitoring.","compensation":"The study covers the cost of treatments, required diagnostics, and management of study-related adverse events (up to $2,000 per patient).

Owners are responsible for pre-enrollment screening costs, including initial consultations and eligibility diagnostics.

No monetary compensation is provided.","links":[],"study_id":21024,"logo_preview_url":"https://yuzu-studypages-prod-east.s3.amazonaws.com/org_logos/ucdavis-veterinary-medicine-logo.png","logo_preview_url_or_none":"https://yuzu-studypages-prod-east.s3.amazonaws.com/org_logos/ucdavis-veterinary-medicine-logo.png","banner_preview_url":"https://yuzu-studypages-prod-east.s3.amazonaws.com/study_banners/276511-a0dc91e7-1ecf-4a1e-a76a-d5a0d1234937.JPG","start_date":"2025-01-27","end_date":"2027-09-10","study_conditions":["Lung Metastases","Canine Cancer","Cancer"],"contact_phone":"+15307541954","target_gender":"B","responsibilities":"<p><strong>Attend Scheduled Visits:</strong></p><ol><li data-list="bullet"><span></span><strong>Pre-enrollment screening (Days -7 to -1):</strong> Initial evaluation, including diagnostic imaging and bloodwork.</li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span><strong>Treatment visits (Days 0, 14, 28, 42, 56, and 70):</strong> Includes physical exams, blood sampling, thoracic radiographs, and antibody administration. Dogs will be required to spend the night at the hospital after the first antibody administration. </li><li data-list="bullet"><span></span><strong>Follow-up monitoring (Days 4, 7, and post-treatment):</strong> Includes physical exams, blood sampling and quality-of-life evaluations.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Monitor Your Dog’s Health:</strong></p><p>Observe for any changes in behavior or health and report adverse events to the study team promptly.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Adhere to Study Protocol:</strong></p><p>Ensure compliance with treatment schedules and follow any instructions provided by the study team.</p>","healthy_volunteer":"N","species":["dogs"],"is_active":true,"video_thumb_url":null,"contact_name":"VCCT","contact_email":"vcct@ucdavis.edu","study_refer_conditions":null,"recruitment_target":10,"locations":[{"lat":"38.5449065","lng":"-121.7405167","route":null,"address":"Davis, CA, USA","country":"United States","locality":"Davis","site_name":"University of California, Davis School of Veterinary Medicine","postal_code":null,"street_number":null,"address_line_2":null,"administrative_area_level_1":"CA"}],"contact_phone_ext":"","content_lang":"en","ai_managed":false,"created_date":"2025-01-28T20:47:05.282059Z","modified_date":"2026-09-11T17:31:11.682848Z","seo_description":null},"investigators":[{"id":1637,"public_display_name":"Sami Al-Nadaf, Assistant Professor","profile_pic":"https://yuzu-studypages-prod-east.s3.amazonaws.com/form-uploads/salnadaf.jpg","organization":"University of California, Davis"},{"id":2701,"public_display_name":"Robert B Rebhun, Professor","profile_pic":"https://yuzu-studypages-prod-east.s3.amazonaws.com/study_investigators/RRPic.jpg","organization":"Surgical & Radiological Sciences"}],"is_draft":false,"multi_content_enabled":false,"feature_can_snooze":true,"is_snoozed":false,"schema_version":3,"google_maps_key":"[REDACTED_GOOGLE_API_KEY]","user_edit_allowed":false,"multi_locations":false,"avma_id":"VCCT-24-012","iacuc_number":"24060","org_study_sites_management_enabled":false,"managed_locations":[]}
